# Force LF line endings on checkout for every platform.
#
# Go tooling assumes LF, and several conformance tests embed golden fixtures
# via go:embed and byte-compare them against raw-string constants. On a Windows
# checkout, core.autocrlf rewrites text files to CRLF: the Go compiler discards
# the \r from raw-string literals, but go:embed keeps the embedded bytes' \r, so
# the two diverge and the conformance gate fails only on the windows-latest CI
# leg. Pinning LF keeps the fixtures byte-stable across all runners.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders: never line-ending-convert the embedded golden fixtures,
# regardless of git's text/binary heuristic — go:embed needs the exact bytes.
bench/cmd/taubench/golden/** -text
